WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.860
Unfortunately at schools, you're required
to learn whatever they teach you and

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.390
then, you know, write a test on it
or, uh, you know, do exercises on it.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.350
All of which I find
unpleasant and unhelpful.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:19.110
I there, Steve Kaufmann here today, I want
to talk about, you know, should you go

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.560
to a language school to learn a language?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.980
If you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe.

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:28.470
You can click on the
bell for notification.

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:29.700
All right.

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:35.250
So the overwhelming majority of
people who study languages who learn

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.670
languages do so I think at schools,
uh, here in Vancouver, we have all

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.410
kinds of schools downtown and elsewhere
where people come to learn English.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.870
People go to Spain to learn Spanish
people, go to China to learn Chinese.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:58.125
And so, and of course there are schools
here, let's say in Vancouver that

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:01.425
teach, uh, French or Arabic or whatever.

00:01:01.735 --> 00:01:05.985
These can range from universities
to all kinds of language schools.

00:01:07.304 --> 00:01:08.715
How can we use these schools?

00:01:08.715 --> 00:01:09.884
How beneficial are they?

00:01:10.965 --> 00:01:11.384
All right.

00:01:11.414 --> 00:01:15.495
This depends entirely on
your own preference like so

00:01:15.495 --> 00:01:16.515
much in language learning.

00:01:16.995 --> 00:01:21.164
Personally, I would not attend a
language school and I'll explain why.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:26.625
What The language school provides
is instruction in the language.

00:01:26.655 --> 00:01:30.794
In other words, explanations
of how the language works.

00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:35.925
The language school provides the
materials, the textbooks, the

00:01:35.925 --> 00:01:39.884
content from which we learn, the
language schools can provide,

00:01:41.445 --> 00:01:43.725
encourage encouragement, motivation.

00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:49.574
The language school provides a social
context where you meet not only

00:01:49.574 --> 00:01:51.345
your teacher, but other students.

00:01:52.035 --> 00:01:53.835
The language school can keep you going.

00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:58.335
So it is possible that for many
people a language school is

00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:00.195
an ideal learning environment.

00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:03.015
Why is that not the case for me?

00:02:03.675 --> 00:02:08.475
Because in so far as explanations
of how the language works,

00:02:09.675 --> 00:02:11.025
that is available everywhere.

00:02:11.055 --> 00:02:17.805
I can Google for grammars in Romania
and Arabic Turkish, any language.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.580
Uh, I can buy a small grammar
book, occasionally leaf through it.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.550
I don't have to learn the structures and
the rules of grammar, uh, on whatever

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.680
order the teacher decides for me.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.990
I can learn these and look these things
up and access the grammar whenever I

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.690
want to on my own schedule on my own.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.535
So I have no need for a teacher to
take me through the explanation of the

00:02:44.535 --> 00:02:46.095
grammar and how the language works.

00:02:46.455 --> 00:02:51.435
Also, as many of, you know, if you've
been listening to me, I believe that the,

00:02:51.435 --> 00:02:55.725
the introduction of grammar, it's not
something that you can get up front that

00:02:55.725 --> 00:02:59.595
explains the, the language to you and then
you can proceed and learn the language.

00:02:59.985 --> 00:03:04.785
Rather it's a matter of getting
a lot of the language in you, uh,

00:03:04.845 --> 00:03:09.465
listening, reading, using LingQ, if
you're using LingQ and then looking

00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:12.195
up items of grammar whenever you want.

00:03:12.195 --> 00:03:16.785
So you might have an initial overview,
forget most of that rules that you saw

00:03:16.785 --> 00:03:21.945
there and then go back time and time
again on your own schedule to refer back

00:03:21.945 --> 00:03:26.685
to explanations of how the language works
when you are curious about something.

00:03:27.495 --> 00:03:31.815
Unfortunately at schools, you're required
to learn whatever they teach you and

00:03:31.815 --> 00:03:36.315
then, you know, write a test on it
or, uh, you know, do exercises on it.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:42.600
All of which I find unpleasant and
unhelpful when it comes to the context,

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:48.480
the content, the materials, again, the
range of language content that's available

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:53.820
on the internet is far, far greater
than what the teacher can provide you.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:59.190
In fact, the best teachers will direct
you to resources on the internet.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.620
Uh, whether it be beginner material,
or at the other end, you know,

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:08.340
movies from Netflix and so forth in
the language that you are learning.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:15.750
So I have no need for a school to provide
the sort of learning content that I need.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.150
I'll go and find that on my own.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:22.260
And, and, uh, but it may well be
that a person who is not as well

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:27.480
organized and finding this kind of
thing would benefit from being at a

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.090
school where there is more discipline.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.730
Now, of course you don't
have to go to a school.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:37.470
You can have an online tutor such as
I have for Persian and that person,

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.780
or Arabic or other languages, and that
person can often be very helpful in

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:48.480
finding or even creating as is the case
with my, uh, Persian tutor, content.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:52.800
So the school can be a source of content,
but that's not the only source of.

00:04:54.559 --> 00:04:57.469
The school provides a social context.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:01.429
You meet other learners, that
has its pluses and minuses.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.729
If you're in a classroom with
10 other people, some people

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:06.320
will be better than you.

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:08.450
Some people will not be as good.

00:05:08.929 --> 00:05:14.750
Um, it can sometimes for some people
it can be motivate, motivating that

00:05:14.929 --> 00:05:18.390
some people are better than them, other
people may be discouraged by the fact

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.650
that other people are better than them.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:24.210
Also listening to people who speak with
a heavy accent or have trouble speaking

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.310
and having to listen through that in a
classroom is not something that I enjoy.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.030
I would far rather just
listen to a native speaker.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:40.130
Who, you know, even if I'm listening on
my AirPods or listening in a movie, in

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:47.880
other words, I can achieve a more sort
of native language listening and reading

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:54.120
context, which is better for me than
sitting in a classroom, listening to

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:58.080
other people, answer questions or interact
with each other or with the teacher.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:03.570
So now granted, you make friends in the
classroom and that's a major motivation.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.680
That can be good.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.669
It can be bad.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:09.809
If I see the students in downtown
Vancouver, who are learning English,

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:13.530
I find the Brazilians get together
with each other and the Mexicans get

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.950
together with each other, then the
Koreans get together with each other.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:23.280
So my question is, are they in fact
using this sort of social connection

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:28.560
opportunities of a language class
in order to practice their language

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.880
and learn the target language?

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.390
Or are they socializing
with people from the same.

00:06:35.185 --> 00:06:37.945
The more time you spend with
the language that you're

00:06:37.945 --> 00:06:39.715
learning, the better you will do.

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:44.515
So if you end up spending time talking
to people in your own language,

00:06:44.545 --> 00:06:48.805
that is time that's taken away from,
you know, learning the language.

00:06:50.425 --> 00:06:55.165
So other disadvantages are of
the school might be that you

00:06:55.165 --> 00:06:56.335
have to travel to the school.

00:06:57.344 --> 00:07:01.245
It can be, if you're traveling to
Salamanca, Spain in order to work on your

00:07:01.245 --> 00:07:05.234
Spanish, or you're going to Guanajuato
to work on your Spanish, or you're

00:07:05.234 --> 00:07:07.435
going to Prague to work on your Czech.

00:07:07.935 --> 00:07:12.375
Then the fact of being in the country
in a place where the language is spoken

00:07:12.614 --> 00:07:14.414
is a great reason to go to a school.

00:07:14.835 --> 00:07:19.995
However, again, are you better off
sitting in a classroom in Guanajuato

00:07:19.995 --> 00:07:27.390
or Salamanca or Prague or being out
in the city interacting with people.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.220
Now it's often difficult.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:33.000
You can't just arrive in Guanajuato
and randomly talk to people.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:38.820
So to that extent, the school provides
you with a ready-made group of people,

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.720
the teachers who are sympathetic to you,
who are going to talk to you in Spanish.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.940
And so all of that is good.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.550
So that's again, it's so that the
secret to making the most of your

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.810
experience at a language school is go
to where the language is spoken, speak

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:58.860
to your teachers, by all means, try to
find people outside the classroom and

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:03.090
spend as little time as possible with
people of the same background as you

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.920
who are learning the target language.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:09.370
Of course the issue with, with
language schools is the cost.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:13.310
So there again, you have to
look at your own learning style.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.980
How, how motivated are you, you
know, intrinsically by yourself?

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.810
To what extent do you need the motivation
and the discipline and the sympathetic ear

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:28.450
of the teachers at the school versus how
capable are you a finding material on your

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.340
own finding people to talk to on your own?

00:08:31.185 --> 00:08:36.735
So I think one can't, it's not a
situation where one answer is sort of

00:08:36.735 --> 00:08:38.805
one, one solution works for everyone.

00:08:39.015 --> 00:08:43.395
I think it's for everyone to
decide how they like to learn how

00:08:43.395 --> 00:08:44.535
they like to spend their time.

00:08:45.045 --> 00:08:49.125
And so, while personally, I wouldn't
go to a language school because

00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:54.495
I would feel that it's sort of
imposes constraints on my language,

00:08:54.525 --> 00:08:56.115
on my, on my language learning.

00:08:56.475 --> 00:08:59.895
And it's, it's an expense that I
would rather forego, do with it.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:06.210
But I think, uh, uh, many people, if
as long as they do enough on their own

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:11.760
outside of the classroom, they can make
a success of learning in the classroom.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:19.770
And probably the success rate is greater
amongst students who go to classrooms

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:26.250
because maybe most people aren't as
motivated as I am, to be perfectly

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:32.400
honest, but I think it's still up to each
person to decide for himself or herself.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.200
Thank you for listening.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.310
And I hope you make the right
decision for yourself when

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:38.900
it comes to langauge schools.

